<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Akinyi can paint a classroom block in <m>{12}</m> days; Otieno can do it in <m>{6}</m> days. Akinyi works alone for <m>{3}</m> days, then Otieno joins and they finish the job together.</p><p>(a) What fraction of the job is still to do when Otieno joins? Give a fraction, for example <c>7/12</c>, or a decimal correct to 3 decimal places.</p><p><fillin characters="6" name="ans1"/>  </p><p>(b) How many more days do they take?</p><p><fillin characters="6" name="ans2"/> days  </p><p>(c) How many days does the whole job take?</p><p><fillin characters="6" name="ans3"/> days  </p><p>Give (b) and (c) exactly or correct to 1 decimal place.</p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>(a) Akinyi does <m>\dfrac{1}{ {12} }</m> of the job a day, so in <m>{3}</m> days <m>{\frac{1}{4}}</m> of it. Still to do: <m>1 - {\frac{1}{4}} = {\frac{3}{4}}</m>.</p><p>(b) Together they do <m>\dfrac{1}{ {12} } + \dfrac{1}{ {6} } = {\frac{1}{4}}</m> of the job a day. More days <m>= {\frac{3}{4}} \div {\frac{1}{4}} = {3}</m>.</p><p>(c) Whole job <m>= {3} + {3} = {6}</m> days.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{3}{4}</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>3</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>6</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>